A||||4||sqoach||Oh Sh!t...what did I just do!?||||11||
Z||000000||sqoach||06-08-2001||08:40 PM||||Ok, I'm checking my rear brake pads on my 86 SC. I have the e-brake bracket off, caliper off. I conclude that the brakes are still good for a while, so I put the caliper back. Now I try to get the e-brake bracket thingy back on and it's not going. After messing with it for a minute, I notice oil leaking out of bolt thingy that holds on that bracket. What happened!? Did I just bust a seal or something??? Now there's a puddle of oil under my wheel.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-08-2001||08:46 PM||||When you were trying to replace the bracket for the E-brake, the screw went into the caliper a little.<BR>Remove the caliper again so you can see what your doing, turn the screw out till you get the round flat part flush with the casing, set the lever in proper position and replace nut. Hopefully the seal wasn't pinched!||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||06-08-2001||09:09 PM||||Yep, that's what happened. Well I'm glad that was an easy fix. Thanks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||06-08-2001||10:59 PM||||No problem, better keep an eye on it for a while though!||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-09-2001||09:27 PM||||Definatly keep an eye on it. The seal usually should not pinch, but it could have gotten nicked by dirt in the hole. That could let it have a slow leak.<P>If the pedal feels even a little softer than before bleed that caliper to make sure it didn't let in any air...||||reg||1
